# No em dashes

Never use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) anywhere in this project.

This applies to:

- User-facing UI copy (headings, labels, error messages, empty states)
- Blog posts and marketing content
- Code comments and JSDoc
- Documentation (`*.md`)

## Use instead

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| `Clause — clause` | `Clause. Clause` or `Clause, clause` |
| `Word—word` (glued) | `Word, word` or `Word: word` |
| `/** API — description */` | `/** API: description */` |

## Examples

```tsx
// Bad
<p>Sign in below — one login for both apps.</p>

// Good
<p>Sign in below. One login for both apps.</p>
```

When editing existing text, remove em dashes rather than swapping them for en dashes (`–`).
